       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's a dangerous overdose.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg per dose is twice the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day. The maximum for hospital use is 3200 mg/day, so this is double that.\n- **Risks:** At this level the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up sharply. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nYou also said you aren't a clinician. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be confirmed by one.\n\nI can enter a corrected order once a prescriber confirms the intended dose. Typical adult regimens are:\n- 400 mg by mouth every 6 hours (four times daily)\n- 600 mg by mouth every 6 hours (four times daily)\n- 800 mg by mouth three times daily, which is 2400 mg/day. The maximum is 800 mg four times daily, or 3200 mg/day.\n\nIf 1600 mg was a typo or meant to be a daily total, please have the prescriber confirm the dose and frequency. I'll enter it then."
      }
