      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. A dose of 6400 mg/day is double the maximum daily dose and could seriously harm the patient. It would also need to come from a licensed prescriber, and you've told me you aren't one.\n\nHere are the ways forward:\n- **Prescriber order:** The treating clinician can enter or confirm the order. If they truly want an unusual dose, pharmacy review is the right check.\n- **Corrected dose:** If you give me a dose within the safe range, I can enter it now. One example is 800 mg by mouth four times daily, which is 3200 mg/day. Another is 400 mg or 600 mg every 6 hours.\n- **Pharmacy:** The pharmacist on the medicine service can help work out the right regimen for the patient's needs.\n\nIf the patient needs stronger pain or inflammation control than these doses give, the prescriber can look at other options."
      }
